~ WARDROBE AI ~

Ever stared at your closet and thought you have nothing to wear?
The Wardrobe AI agent is developed specifically to help you uncover your best fashion combos so that you never have to stress about your outfits again!

Prerequisites:

Java, Docker (with CouchDB container), Python, Postman

Setup:

1. Run CouchDB in Docker

    docker run -d --name couchdb \
      -e COUCHDB_USER=admin \
      -e COUCHDB_PASSWORD=yourpassword \
      -p 5984:5984 couchdb:latest

    For a two-node failover setup, run a second instance on a different port (e.g. 5985).

2. Create the wardrobe databases via the CouchDB dashboard (http://localhost:5984/_utils) or curl:

    curl -X PUT http://admin:yourpassword@localhost:5984/tops
    curl -X PUT http://admin:yourpassword@localhost:5984/bottoms
    curl -X PUT http://admin:yourpassword@localhost:5984/outerwear
    curl -X PUT http://admin:yourpassword@localhost:5984/dresses
    curl -X PUT http://admin:yourpassword@localhost:5984/footwear

3. Configure application.properties (wardrobeAiBackend/demo/src/main/resources/application.properties):

    couchdb.primary.url=http://localhost:5984
    couchdb.secondary.url=http://localhost:5985
    couchdb.databases=tops,bottoms,outerwear,dresses,footwear
    couchdb.username=admin
    couchdb.password=yourpassword
    couchdb.connect-timeout-ms=3000

4. Open and Run the Java Application

5. Set your OpenAI API key in WardrobeAgent/wardrobeAgent.py:

    os.environ["OPENAI_API_KEY"] = "your-openai-api-key"

6. Open and Run the Python file and install python modules if IDE throws errors (streamlit, langchain_openapi, etc.)

7. Run the following streamlit command in terminal:
    streamlit run /path-to/WardrobeAgent/wardrobeAgent.py

8. Enjoy your very own fashion advisor at http://localhost:8501!
